Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Tetrahedron Zonofication", "Section",
 Evaluatable->False,
 AspectRatioFixed->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"373bc0d2-cb70-424c-b3f3-919e28f422e4"],

Cell["Truncated Rhombic Dodecahedron", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a2e221d9-dc5e-4d3f-a18a-829d91fd9d40"],

Cell["\<\
This has as its generators the seven axes of symmetry of a tetrahedron. Since \
its generators are the union of those for the cube and the rhombic \
dodecahedron, it is the Minkowski sum of those two shapes.  The hexagons can \
not be regular, although they do have all sides the same length, since three \
regular hexagons would meet in a flat solid angle instead of the corners \
here.  Although this shape does not fill space on its own, it can be combined \
with cubes in a regular space-filling pattern. (Eppstein).\
\>", "Text",
 Evaluatable->False,
 AspectRatioFixed->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"451a959e-f6de-4b33-afed-80e84dbc28d7"],

